XN0b25lNDUzMDQz","number":7,"title":"3.0.0","description":"New major release that breaks compatibility with 2.x\r\n\r\n- PHP5.4.19+\r\n- New ORM & behaviors.\r\n- Improved Routing\r\n- PSR-0 and composer support.\r\n- Simpler configuration and bootstrapping.\r\n- Improved configuration handling.\r\n- Improved bake.\r\n\r\nSee [the roadmap](http://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/wiki/3.0-roadmap) for more details.","creator":null,"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":2464,"state":"closed","created_at":"2013-10-11T20:56:23Z","updated_at":"2015-12-17T03:00:48Z","due_on":"2015-03-22T04:00:00Z","closed_at":"2015-03-23T01:02:41Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2014-03-18T20:30:36Z","updated_at":"2014-03-18T21:55:53Z","closed_at":"2014-03-18T21:55:53Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Create a table with date, time, or datetime field. Add a validation rule on it. It will fail because the entity marshals it into a DateTime object and the validation rules expect a string.\n\nMarshalling sort of checks for validity already, if its not a valid string format that DateTime can parse it throws an exception and the marshaller returns the string back instead of a `DateTime` object\n\nI'm not sure if a sane solution would be to add an early return to the core validation rules if `$check` is a `DateTime` object because the validation rules seem to be more of checking if a **_string**_ is in a **_specific**_ format.\n","closed_by":{"login":"markstory","id":24086,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MDg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory","html_url":"https://github.com/markstory","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/followi